<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila stocks falls 2.77 pct on property fears.</title>
<headline>Manila stocks falls 2.77 pct on property fears.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>------------------------- April 22 ----------------------------</p>
<p>* Empire East, Megaworld lead losers</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Manila stocks tumbled in late trade on Tuesday due to a selldown on Empire East Land Holdngs Inc and its parent Megaworld Properties &amp; Holdings Inc, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Panic selling in Empire East and Megaworld spilled over to other issues,&quot; said Henry Ong, research head at Sapphire Securities. The main index fell below its 2,880 support to 2,863.27, down 81.71 points or 2.77 percent.</p>
</text>
